{"id": "EUVD-2026-104398", "enisaUuid": "333da2fb-7888-304f-90d9-3ea7f333c331", "description": "NocoBase @nocobase/plugin-collection-sql through 2.2.28 contains an SQL injection vulnerability that allows privileged users to store unvalidated SQL by bypassing checkSQL() through the sqlCollection:setFields action. Attackers holding the collection-sql snippet can replace a benign collection query with dangerous statements executed on reload, reading pg_shadow password hashes or calling pg_read_file.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T15:28:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T16:33:44", "baseScore": 8.6, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/nocobase/nocobase/issues/10629", "https://github.com/nocobase/nocobase/blob/v2.2.28/packages/plugins/@nocobase/plugin-collection-sql/src/server/resources/sql.ts#L14-L104", "https://github.com/nocobase/nocobase", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/nocobase-plugin-collection-sql-through-2.2.28-sql-injection-via-sqlcollection-setfields"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-112306", "GHSA-j67h-xf8r-r323"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.31, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "e1c428ae-9c72-3225-8a04-0a8785af552f", "product": {"name": "nocobase", "vendor": {"name": "nocobase"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.2.28"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "75ad0b54-1206-32e7-9145-6401b11db6ba", "vendor": {"name": "nocobase"}}], "isExploited": false}